  "question": {
    "text": "Two identical particles each of mass ' $m$ ' go round a circle of radius $a$ under the action of their mutual gravitational attraction. The angular speed of each particle will be:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "3KwgM",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{\\frac{G m}{2 a^3}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "pHzMs",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{\\frac{\\mathrm{Gm}}{8 \\mathrm{a}^3}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "jthcR",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{\\frac{G m}{4 a^3}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "1bPEl",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{\\frac{G m}{a^3}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Radius of circle, $\\mathrm{r}=\\mathrm{a}$<br />Centrifugal force, $F=m \\omega^2 r$<br />$\\begin{aligned}<br />& \\Rightarrow \\frac{\\mathrm{Gmm}}{(2 \\mathrm{a})^2}=\\mathrm{m} \\omega^2 \\mathrm{a} \\\\<br />& \\left(\\because \\mathrm{F}=\\frac{\\mathrm{G} \\mathrm{M} \\mathrm{M}_2}{\\mathrm{~d}}\\right)<br />\\end{aligned}$<br />Here $M_1=m ; M_2=m$ and $d=2 a$<br />$\\Rightarrow$ angular speed, $\\omega=\\sqrt{\\frac{G m}{4 a^3}}$",
    "image": null
  },
